  "description": "The Senhance Surgical System is a teleoperated multiport robotic platform for minimally invasive surgery developed by Asensus Surgical (originally TransEnterix). The system features up to four independent bedside robotic arm carts, an open surgeon console with a 3D display and infrared eye-tracking camera navigation, and reusable 3 mm, 5 mm, and 10 mm laparoscopic instruments with haptic force sensing. Cleared by the US FDA and CE marked for abdominal, gynecological, urological, and pediatric laparoscopy, an end-of-service timeline was initiated following KARL STORZ's acquisition of Asensus in 2024.",
